{{Quote|Sir, sensors triggered in Hangar 718. We're searching the area.|A stormtrooper, to Kylo Ren|<ref name="TFA" />}}
'''Hangar 718''' was a [[hangar]] at [[Starkiller Base]], the [[First Order]]'s [[superweapon]]<ref name="TFA" /> built into the [[planet]] [[Ilum]].<ref name="TROS" /> In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Date" /> [[sensor]]s at the hangar were triggered during the [[scavenger]] [[Rey Skywalker|Rey's]] attempted escape from the base. A [[Unidentified First Order stormtrooper (Starkiller Base)|First Order stormtrooper]] notified<ref name="TFA" /> First Order leader<ref name="TROS" /> [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]] of the alert and that the area was being searched.<ref name="TFA" />

Later, an [[Unidentified First Order officer (Starkiller Base) 3|officer]] informed Ren that Rey was not found in the hangar but that all [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtroopers]] were on alert. Ren then ordered the [[First Order officer|officer]] to place all hangars on lockdown to prevent the fugitive from escaping aboard a [[starship]]. Soon after, the hangar was destroyed when Starkiller Base exploded during an [[Battle of Starkiller Base|attack]] by the [[Resistance]].<ref name="TFA" /> The hangar was included as a location on Starkiller Base in the [[book]] ''[[Galactic Explorer's Guide]]'', [[author]]ed by the [[pirate]] [[Hondo Ohnaka]] and his [[RA-7 protocol droid|protocol droid]] [[DK-RA-43]] at some point after the [[Battle of Crait]]<ref name="Explorer's Guide">''[[Star Wars: The Galactic Explorer's Guide]]''</ref> in [[34 ABY]].<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|She was not found in hangar 718, Yet ev'ry trooper stayeth on alert.|A trooper, to Kylo Ren in ''William Shakespeare's The Force Doth Awaken: Star Wars Part the Seventh''|<ref name="Shake">''[[William Shakespeare's The Force Doth Awaken: Star Wars Part the Seventh]]''</ref>}}
The hangar was first mentioned in the [[2015]] [[Star Wars saga|film]] [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']],<ref name="TFA" /> the first installment in the [[sequel trilogy]].<ref name="YBY">''[[Star Wars Year By Year: A Visual History, New Edition]]''</ref> In the [[2017]] [[Canon|non-canon]] book ''[[William Shakespeare's The Force Doth Awaken: Star Wars Part the Seventh]]'' by [[Ian Doescher]], which retells the events of the film, Kylo Ren is informed of Rey not being found in Hangar 718 by a [[trooper]]<ref name="Shake" /> instead of a First Order [[officer]].<ref name="TFA" />

The [[De Agostini]] [[Star Wars Encyclopedia (series)|''Star Wars Encyclopedia'']] issue "[[Battle Stations of the Empire and the First Order]],"<ref name="Battle">{{EncyclopediaCite|Battle Stations of the Empire and the First Order}}</ref> which was released on [[June 1]], [[2021]],<ref name="Release">{{DeAgostini|lang=es|url=libros-comics/enciclopedia-star-wars|text=Enciclopedia Star Wars}}</ref> states that<ref name="Battle" /> the [[smuggler]]<ref name="TFA" /> [[Han Solo]],<ref name="Battle" /> accompanied by his co-[[pilot]] [[Chewbacca]] and stormtrooper [[Desertion|defector]] [[Finn]],<ref name="TFA" /> triggered the [[Alarm system|alarm]] in Hangar 718 during his infiltration of the base<ref name="Battle" /> with the aim of shutting down the facility's [[Planetary shield|shields]]. However, as depicted in ''The Force Awakens'', Ren was alerted to the alarm before Solo had entered Starkiller Base.<ref name="TFA" /> This article assumes the encyclopedia is in error.

